Chapter: WebGpu

 The browser's GPU bridge (docs/Designs/Active/Apps/InBrowserDiffusion.md,
 stage 2): codex/os/kernel/GpuBridge.codex's buffer and launch contract over
 WebGPU. The records and argument helpers are the native ones; the stubs below
 are bound to the HTML plug's runtime and never emitted. A launch takes the WGSL
 plug's module text and a kernel's entry name. What the browser cannot answer
 at once takes a callback: opening the device, reading a buffer back, and
 uploading a range of a picked file.

 We say:

Section: Records

  GpuGrid = record {
    gx : Integer,
    gy : Integer,
    gz : Integer,
    bx : Integer,
    by : Integer,
    bz : Integer,
    shared : Integer
  }

  GpuParam = record {
    kind : Integer,
    handle : Integer,
    value : Integer
  }

  gpu-arg-buf : Integer, Integer -> GpuParam
  gpu-arg-buf (h) (off) = GpuParam { kind = 0, handle = h, value = off }

  gpu-arg-u32 : Integer -> GpuParam
  gpu-arg-u32 (v) = GpuParam { kind = 1, handle = 0, value = v }

  gpu-arg-f32 : Real -> GpuParam
  gpu-arg-f32 (v) = GpuParam { kind = 1, handle = 0, value = gpu-f32-bits v }

  gpu-dt-f32 : Integer = 1

  gpu-dt-f16 : Integer = 2

Section: Bridge

  gpu-open-then : (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-open-then (cb) = 0

  gpu-buf-alloc : Integer -> Integer
  gpu-buf-alloc (bytes) = 0

  gpu-buf-free : Integer -> Boolean
  gpu-buf-free (h) = False

  gpu-buf-copy-range : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gpu-buf-copy-range (src) (src-off) (dst) (dst-off) (bytes) = False

 The worker returns a native-word noise bank in a GPU buffer. Its Wasm arena
 is job-local and its worker is terminated before the callback.
 Progress repeats (0, 1) during preparation; a negative result cancels it.

  gpu-noise-bank-then : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, (Integer, Integer -> Integer), (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-noise-bank-then (module) (seed) (n) (sampler) (steps) (progress) (cb) = 0

  gpu-buf-write-words : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  gpu-buf-write-words (h) (off) (words) = False

  gpu-buf-download-then : Integer, Integer, Integer, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-buf-download-then (h) (off) (bytes) (cb) = 0

  gpu-buf-upload-then : Integer, Integer, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-buf-upload-then (h) (dst-off) (name) (file-off) (count) (src-dt) (dst-dt) (cb) = 0

 An f32 3 x hh x w image in h drawn into the canvas sel names, each channel
 clamp ((v + 1) / 2, 0, 1) * 255 rounded; the callback runs once it is drawn.

  gpu-buf-show-then : Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-buf-show-then (h) (w) (hh) (sel) (cb) = 0

 The callback runs once every launch queued before the call has finished on
 the device.

  gpu-done-then : (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-done-then (cb) = 0

 Pooled buffers at invocation are removed from reuse, then destroyed after
 queued work completes. Active handles remain valid. Empty text is success.

  gpu-trim-then : (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  gpu-trim-then (cb) = 0

 Milliseconds since the page opened.

  clock-ms : Integer -> Integer
  clock-ms (z) = 0

  gpu-launch : Text, Text, GpuGrid, List GpuParam -> Integer
  gpu-launch (code) (name) (g) (ps) = 0

  gpu-error : Integer -> Text
  gpu-error (x) = ""

  gpu-f32-bits : Real -> Integer
  gpu-f32-bits (v) = 0

 Browser pickers answer once with their selection or JSON { error, code }.
 Cancellation has code AbortError; absent directory-picker support has
 NotSupportedError. A failed or empty writable-folder selection preserves
 the previous write handle.

  pick-file-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  pick-file-then (accept) (cb) = 0

 A folder the user picks, every file under it ending in ext registered as
 pick-file-then registers one; the callback gets a JSON list of { name,
 path, size }, sorted by path.

  pick-dir-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  pick-dir-then (ext) (cb) = 0

  file-read-then : Text, Integer, Integer, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-read-then (name) (off) (bytes) (cb) = 0

  file-url : Text -> Text
  file-url (name) = ""

  dir-open-then : (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  dir-open-then (cb) = 0

  clock-utc-text : Integer -> Text
  clock-utc-text (offset-ms) = ""

  file-delete-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-delete-then (path) (cb) = 0

  canvas-save-then : Text, Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  canvas-save-then (selector) (path) (cb) = 0

  file-exists-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-exists-then (path) (cb) = 0

  file-sha256-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-sha256-then (name) (cb) = 0

  audio-analyze-then : Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  audio-analyze-then (name) (cb) = 0

  file-write-then : Text, Text, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-write-then (path) (text) (cb) = 0

 A byte-heap range and selected directory are snapshotted at the call.
 Saves in this page are serialized and check that the file is absent.
 Callback JSON carries
 ok, name, path and size; name is registered for file-read-then and file-url.

  file-save-bytes-then : Text, Integer, Integer, (Text -> Integer) -> Integer
  file-save-bytes-then (path) (address) (bytes) (cb) = 0
